u}{y(1-y)}dy\&=N_{e}\int^{x} rac{d\ln[\overline{W}(y)]}{dy}dy+2N_{e}\mu\int^{x} rac{1}{y}dy-2N_{e}
u\int^{x} rac{1}{1-y}dy\&=N_{e}\ln[\overline{W}(x)]+2N_{e}\mu\ln(x)+2N_{e}
u\ln(1-x)\end{aligned} $$ Hence $$ G(x)=\exp\left[-2\int_{}^{x} rac{m(y)}{v(y)}dyight]=\overline{W}(x)^{-2N_{e}}x^{-4N_{e}\mu}\left(1-xight)^{-4N_{e}
u} $$ If we substitute this expression for $ G(x) $ into Equation A1.11, it returns the stationary distribution as $$ \varphi(x)=C\overline{W}(x)^{2N_{e}}x^{4N_{e}\mu-1}\left(1-xight)^{4N_{e}
u-1}\quad for0<x<1 $$ (A1.15) a result first due to Wright (1931), obtained using a different approach.

